# A window (a building system in a wall's opening) is picked in the plan
# where it stands: on it at once, and after its wall moved, at its new place
# and no longer at its old one (`the bim footprint gap of`, as placed).
import examples/bim-slice/bim_stair.dl

function check window pick {boolean:condition} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

# How far plan point (x, y) lies from system `systemId`'s footprint.
function the window pick gap at {a 64 bit floating-point number:x} {a 64 bit floating-point number:y} to {a 64 bit integer:systemId} in {bim model record:modelValue}:
    execute:
        set found to the bim curtain index of systemId in modelValue
        return the bim footprint gap of (a cad vector2 with x x and y y) to (the item at found's position in (modelValue's curtains's values)) in modelValue

set modelValue to an empty bim model
set target to the address of modelValue
set ground to add bim level named (the string form of "Ground") at 0.0 with height 3.0 to target
set layerValues to an empty list of a bim layer record
append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "brick", 0.1)) to layerValues
set brickType to add bim wall type named (the string form of "Brick 100") with layerValues to target
set wallId to add bim wall typed brickType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y 0.0) to target
set windowType to add bim opening type named (the string form of "Window 1200") sized 1.2 by 1.5 with sill 0.9 and frame 0.05 to target
set openingId to add bim opening typed windowType in wallId at 3.0 to target
set systemId to add bim system in opening openingId with joint (10 as a 64 bit integer) in bays of 0.6 by 0.75 of (the string form of "wood") to target
check window pick ((the window pick gap at 3.0 0.0 to systemId in modelValue) = 0.0) named (the string form of "picked on it where it stands")

set wallFound to the bim wall index of wallId in modelValue
set movedWall to the item at wallFound's position in (modelValue's walls's values)
set movedWall's start to a cad vector2 with x 2.0 and y 1.0
set movedWall's finish to a cad vector2 with x 8.0 and y 1.0
replace item at index wallFound's position in (target's walls's values) with movedWall
check window pick ((the window pick gap at 5.0 1.0 to systemId in modelValue) = 0.0) named (the string form of "after the wall moved, picked at its new place")
check window pick ((the window pick gap at 3.0 0.0 to systemId in modelValue) > 0.5) named (the string form of "and not at its old place")
